// Messages every service of the operator API shares, and the rules of the
// whole API.
//
// The operator API is what an operator, the command line and the panel use
// to drive the control plane. It replaces the operator's HTTP/JSON routes;
// the node protocol, the webhook triggers, /healthz and /metrics stay HTTP
// and are not part of this package.
//
// Transport and authentication, for every RPC:
//
//   - gRPC over TLS, the server certificate issued by the fleet CA.
//   - The bearer token in the metadata key `authorization`, as
//     `authorization: Bearer <token>` (the same token the HTTP API takes in
//     the Authorization header). A missing or wrong token is
//     UNAUTHENTICATED. A node certificate opens nothing here.
//   - The actor, on the RPCs that decide (ApproveTask, DenyTask, DecideTask),
//     in the metadata key `x-axlr-actor` (the HTTP API's X-Axlr-Actor
//     header), which a bot's approvers are compared with. DecideTask's
//     `decided_by` field says the same; when both are given and differ the
//     call fails with INVALID_ARGUMENT. Neither: the control plane's own
//     actor, which a bot that lists approvers refuses.
//   - Large messages: gRPC's default is 4 MiB. Artifacts and transcripts go
//     in chunks (see ExecutionsService); a server of this API raises its
//     send limit for the activity snapshot (see ActivityService).
//
// Errors are gRPC statuses with an ErrorDetail in the status details. The
// kinds are the ones the HTTP API named:
//
//	kind              gRPC code
//	not_found         NOT_FOUND
//	validation        INVALID_ARGUMENT
//	state             FAILED_PRECONDITION
//	approval_expired  FAILED_PRECONDITION
//	conflict          ABORTED
//	forbidden         PERMISSION_DENIED
//	unauthorized      UNAUTHENTICATED
//	too_large         RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED
//	internal          INTERNAL
//
// Conventions: instants are google.protobuf.Timestamp, durations
// google.protobuf.Duration, money is double US dollars with a separate
// `cost_unknown` flag (the cost is then zero and means "not known", never
// "free"). Status and kind vocabularies (task status, execution outcome,
// event type, trigger type...) are strings documented by the domain, not
// enums: the control plane adds values without a new contract. An empty
// string field is "absent" unless it says otherwise.

